<mxCell id="a_note_login" value="&lt;b&gt;How tokens are obtained&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• POST /api/user/login/ – identifier may be e-mail, username or phone (MultiAccountAuthBackend). All previously outstanding refresh tokens of the user are blacklisted on login.&lt;br&gt;• One institution → tokens with current_institution. Several → 202 + temporary tokens, then POST /api/user/select-institution/.&lt;br&gt;• POST /api/user/token/refresh/ – refresh lifetime 2 h, rotation + blacklist.&lt;br&gt;• Google sign-in: /api/user/auth/google/url/ and /callback/.&lt;br&gt;• OTP / password reset endpoints are AllowAny." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffde7;strokeColor=#bfa900;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1280" y="800" width="380" height="240" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
<mxCell id="a_inferred" value="&lt;b&gt;Inferred – verify&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• Several partner-facing views are declared &lt;i&gt;AllowAny&lt;/i&gt; and call PartnerSystemAuthentication themselves inside the handler; whether every such view enforces the key should be reviewed per view (see API map).&lt;br&gt;• /api/user/taskmgt-user-state-data/ is AllowAny but reads request.user.&lt;br&gt;• GoogleAuthCallbackView reads settings.GOOGLE_AUTH_REDIRECT_URL, which is not defined in core/settings.py." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cc0000;fontColor=#cc0000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1280" y="1080" width="380" height="190" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
