<mxCell id="rr18" value="dynamic membership by permission code" style="edgeStyle=orthogonalEdgeStyle;rounded=1;html=1;endArrow=block;endFill=1;fontSize=10;labelBackgroundColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#444444;dashed=1;exitX=0.5;exitY=0;exitDx=0;exitDy=0;entryX=1;entryY=0.5;entryDx=0;entryDy=0;entryY=0.8;" edge="1" parent="1" source="r_ag" target="r_perm"><mxGeometry relative="1" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
<mxCell id="r_note" value="&lt;b&gt;How it works&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;1. Roles bundle permissions (RolePermission). Users get roles (UserRole) directly or through staff groups.&lt;br&gt;2. Role/assignment changes are &lt;b&gt;materialised&lt;/b&gt; into UserPermission rows per institution membership by users/services.py (PermissionSyncService, RoleAssignmentService) and the Celery tasks in users/tasks.py.&lt;br&gt;3. Checks read only UserPermission: CustomUser.has_permission(code, institution).&lt;br&gt;4. Role, UserRole, RolePermission and StaffGroup are approvable (approval_status lifecycle).&lt;br&gt;5. Permission codes are seeded from users/fixtures/permissions.json." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffde7;strokeColor=#bfa900;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1500" y="250" width="400" height="280" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell>
<mxCell id="r_inferred" value="&lt;b&gt;Inferred – verify&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;The exact rule for how StaffGroupRole feeds UserPermission was not traced line by line; verify in users/services.py. Django's built-in groups/user_permissions tables exist (PermissionsMixin) but the custom tables above are what the API checks." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;dashed=1;fillColor=#ffffff;strokeColor=#cc0000;fontColor=#cc0000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1500" y="570" width="400" height="150" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
