<mxCell id="p_note" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;• A tuple of codes means “any one is enough”.&lt;br&gt;• Django superusers pass has_perm() (admin site), but has_permission() itself only has the owner bypass.&lt;br&gt;• The frontend hides pages/controls with the same codes (module.json requiredPermissions); the backend check is authoritative." style="shape=note;size=14;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacing=8;fontSize=11;fillColor=#fffde7;strokeColor=#bfa900;fontColor=#000000;" vertex="1" parent="1"><mxGeometry x="1260" y="330" width="360" height="190" as="geometry"></mxGeometry></mxCell></root></mxGraphModel></diagram>
